        <body>
            <div xml:id="d239-a1">

                <pb facs="0313" n="231" sameAs="frus:frus1865p3/pg231"/>

                <head>No. 1.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <p>I have the honor to state in writing that, upon my arrival at Kioto, <hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">I</hi> fully represented the circumstances of the
                    relations with the treaty powers, as previously stated to you at the interview
                    with my colleagues—the meaning of all of which was understood—wherefore
                    everything, as hitherto, will be strictly observed; but now an important
                    opportunity is presented to tranquillize the public feeling—the order for
                    despatching troops for the punishment of Choshu having been issued, it is,
                    therefore, desirable that you will note this first.</p>
                <p>With respect and esteem.</p>
                <closer><dateline rendition="#float-left"><date calendar="japanese-nengō gregorian"
                            when="1864-11-22">The 23d day of the 10th month of the first year of
                            Gengi, (Né) (November 22, 1864</date>.)</dateline>
                    <lb/>
                    <signed>ABE BUNGO NO KAMI.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His Excellency <hi rendition="#small-caps">Egbert H. Pruyn,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Resident of the United States of America,
                            &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
